From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:32:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Let other modules make and subclass CGImage

UIKit on Linux (Iris's OpenUIKit) gives UIImage.cgImage a CGImage that
carries the encoded image its renderer draws. CGImage had no public
initializer and could not be subclassed outside this module.
---
 Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/CGImage.swift | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/CGImage.swift b/Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/CGImage.swift
index d3b5779..c16304c 100644
--- a/Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/CGImage.swift
+++ b/Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/CGImage.swift
@@ -4,7 +4,11 @@
 //
 //  Created by Kyle on 1/11/26.
 
-public class CGImage: Hashable {
+// Iris: open, with a public initializer, so that UIKit on Linux (Iris's OpenUIKit) can make
+// images that carry what its renderer draws.
+open class CGImage: Hashable {
+    public init() {}
+
     public func hash(into hasher: inout Hasher) {
         hasher.combine(ObjectIdentifier(self))
     }
